# .dockerignore: files in the build context that never reach the image.
# Two reasons to list something: it is a SECRET (it must never be baked into an image layer) or it is
# DEAD WEIGHT (it makes the image bigger and the build slower, and changing it busts the layer cache).

# ---- Secrets: anyone who can pull the image can read every layer, so these must never be copied in ----
.env
.env.*
*cookies*.json
# Redfin login cookies (redfin/chrome_cookies.json). Also matched by *cookies*.json above, kept explicit
redfin/chrome_cookies.json
redfin/redfin_profile/
redfin_profile/

# ---- Version control: the whole history, often bigger than the code itself, and not needed to run ----
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# ---- Build output and local junk: regenerated or machine-specific ----
_site
build_site.py
# "**/" = at any depth. Without it a pattern only matches at the top of the project, so redfin/.pytest_cache or
# app/__pycache__ would slip through.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/output
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
htmlcov/
.coverage
*.log

# ---- Virtual environments: huge, and built for the wrong OS (Windows binaries do not run in Linux) ----
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ---- Tests, docs and scraper-only code: the web app does not use them at run time ----
redfin/tests/
redfin/docs/
redfin/scripts/
# The scraper's URL queue (the web app never reads it)
redfin/data/queue/
test/
docs/

# ---- Editor, assistant and OS files ----
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
redfin/CLAUDE.md
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- Docker's own files: no reason to copy them into the image ----
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
